    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Parks",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6441\n\nSPONSOR: O'MARA\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act in relation to authorizing the town of Ithaca,\ncounty of Tompkins, to alienate and convey certain parcels of land used\nas parklands\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would authorize the town of Ithaca to transfer and convey at\nfair market value certain parkland for the purpose of expanding a child\ncare building and installing, operating and maintaining a septic system,\nprovided that the town of Ithaca dedicate an amount equal to or greater\nthan the fair market value of the parkland being alienated toward the\nacquisition of new parklands.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 authorizes the town of Ithaca to transfer and convey certain\nparklands for the purpose of expanding a child care building and\ninstalling, operating and maintaining a septic system.\n\nSection 2 places a condition on the parkland alienation authorization\ncontained in Section 1, only taking effect if the town of Ithaca dedi-\ncates an amount equal to or greater than the fair market value of the\nparkland being alienated toward the acquisition of new parklands and/or\ncapital improvements to existing park and recreation facilities.\n\nSection 3 provides the boundaries of the parkland to be alienated based\non a map of the property.\n\nSection 4 conditions the alienation authorized by this act to be effec-\ntive only upon compliance with federal requirements, if the town of\nIthaca received any funding or assistance from the federal government\nfor the purchase, maintenance or improvement of the parklands described\nin Section 3.\n\nSection 5 provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe town of Ithaca seeks authorization to transfer a local ballfield and\nassociated recreational parkland, which is currently subject to a town\neasement, located at the Coddington Road Community Center (CRCC). CRCC\nplans a significant expansion of their main facility to provide enhanced\nchild care services, and to install a larger septic system. This expan-\nsion necessarily infringes upon the existing parklands. Thus, the town\nof Ithaca, under the parameters of this legislation, will transfer the\nexisting parkland to CCRC and acquire new parkland in another location\non CCRC land, allowing for both the expected recreational opportunities\nat the community center, and the expansion of CRCC facilities.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
